      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The danger with head bumps, even without immediate symptoms, is the possibility of internal bleeding or swelling that might not show up right away. Because Eliquis prevents clotting, any internal injury could present different risks than in someone not on blood thinners. It's not about causing a panic, but rather ensuring that the protective anti-coagulant medication doesn't worsen any undetected injury. Please err on the side of caution and consult with a medical professional.",
      "source": "target",
